  "question": "Calculate the area bounded by $y = |x|$ and $y = 4$.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "$y=4$ intersects $y=|x|$ at $x=-4,4$.<br /><br />Area $=\\int_{-4}^{4}(4-|x|)dx$.<br /><br />By symmetry $=2\\int_{0}^{4}(4-x)dx$.<br /><br />$=2[4x-\\frac{x^2}{2}]_{0}^{4}=16$.<br /><br />Hence area is $16$ square units.",
